# R47 Track B — PER-ARM POSITIVE CONTROL for the register-at-birth conversion.
#
# CELL: arm = closure-STRUCT local (`calls.rs`, `__Closure_N__call`) ·
# disposition = the call result is TRANSFERRED ONWARD into a container that
# outlives it, and read back afterwards.
#
# ⚠ WHY THIS SHAPE AND NOT AN EASIER ONE — THIS IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE
# FIXTURE. Registering a value for drop at its birth is only safe if exactly
# one owner ends up freeing it. The obvious way to test the "exactly one" half
# is to let the result die where it was made — but both release paths in the
# runtime SELF-NULL BY DESIGN (`gorget_string_free` zeroes the `Str` struct
# after the dealloc, explicitly "so double-free is safe"; `gorget_array_free`
# nulls `data`/`len`/`cap`), so a second release THROUGH THE SAME SLOT is a
# silent no-op and the program stays green while being wrong. A double free is
# observable ONLY when the value ends up in a SECOND LIVE SLOT before both are
# released. This fixture pushes into a Vector and reads the elements back —
# which turns out NOT to produce that second live slot, because the push
# MOVE-ZEROES the source; see the paragraph below, which is the honest result
# of trying to make this fixture fail.
#
# ⚠ GREEN AT HEAD AND AFTER, AND I COULD NOT MAKE IT RED — WHICH IS THE
# FINDING, NOT AN EXCUSE. Two deliberate breaks were built and run against
# this shape: (1) `call_indirect_tracked` made to register the result TWICE,
# and (2) the enum/struct ownership transfer (`emit_enum_init_owned`'s
# post-init unregister) disabled. Both left this program CLEAN 3/3. The reason
# is the mechanism this whole net is built around: at THIS consuming position
# the transfer either zeroes the source slot (`move_zero`, the collection and
# bare-assign paths) or removes its registration, and a second `drop_if_alive`
# through the SAME slot is a no-op because `gorget_string_free` self-nulls by
# design. So an over-registration is not merely unobserved here, it is
# structurally absorbed — and this fixture pins that the conversion did not
# disturb the consuming position's value behaviour or introduce corruption.
# The direction that CAN be observed is pinned by the three
# `combinator_*_transferred_no_double_free.gg` controls, where the adapter's
# Move-assign leaves the pointer in a SECOND LIVE SLOT: those go RED (ASan
# `attempting double-free`, 3/3) against the conversion without its
# compensating transfer.
#
# INSTRUMENT: `security_safe_no_leak`, C lane only (ASan is a no-op under
# `--backend=llvm`). Fire count at this arm: 2 calls, both
# `calls.rs` closure-struct arm, callee `__Closure_0__call`.
from std.collections import Vector

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    auto f = (): mk("hel", "lo")
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push(f())
    v.push(f())
    print(v.len())
    print(v[0])
    print(v[1])
